# --- Guided practice
guide-basics-name = Learn the basics
guide-basics-blurb = Play, split, delete and undo on a sample video.
guide-basics-step1 = Start here. Press Space to play and pause.
guide-basics-step2 = Put the playhead here and press S to split the clip in two.
guide-basics-step3 = Click a clip, then press Delete. Press ⌘Z to bring it back.
guide-basics-step4 = Drag a clip's edge to trim it. Hold ⌥ for fine steps.
guide-basics-step5 = Press ⌘K and ask the AI editor to add a title.
guide-colour-name = Colour practice
guide-colour-blurb = Three shots that do not match. Make them look like one scene.
guide-colour-step1 = Shot 1 is the reference. Look at it first.
guide-colour-step2 = This shot is too blue. Select it, open Inspector, Adjust, Colour and raise Temperature.
guide-colour-step3 = This shot is too warm and bright. Lower Temperature and Exposure. Turn on the scopes to check.
guide-titles-name = Titles and motion
guide-titles-blurb = Edit a title, give it an entry motion and keep it readable.
guide-titles-step1 = Select the title and type your own text in Inspector, Text.
guide-titles-step2 = Open the Motions section of the Library and drop one on the lower third.
guide-titles-step3 = Check the title is readable over the picture. Use Safe areas in the viewer.
guide-audio-name = Audio practice
guide-audio-blurb = Balance voice and music, and fade the ending.
guide-audio-step1 = Play from here. The music is too loud under the voice.
guide-audio-step2 = Select the music, open Inspector, Audio and lower the Volume to about -14 dB.
guide-audio-step3 = Set a Fade out so the music ends smoothly.

# --- Tour
tour-step = Step { $n } of { $total }
tour-finished = Tour finished. Press F1 at any time for help.
tour-welcome-title = Welcome to Zornov
tour-welcome-body = A quick tour of the editor, about a minute. Use the arrow keys or the buttons. Press Escape to leave. You can replay it from Help.
tour-library-title = Library
tour-library-body = Your media, text styles, motions, effects, looks and sounds. Click an item to add it, or drag it onto the timeline. The AI section talks to the AI editor.
tour-viewer-title = Viewer
tour-viewer-body = The picture at the playhead. Press Space to play. J, K and L play backwards, stop and play forwards.
tour-inspector-title = Inspector
tour-inspector-body = The settings of the selected clip: position, colour, audio, speed, animation. Select a clip on the timeline to see them.
tour-timeline-title = Timeline
tour-timeline-body = Your clips in time. S splits at the playhead, M adds a marker, and the left and right arrows step one frame. Everything can be undone with ⌘Z.
tour-workspaces-title = Workspaces
tour-workspaces-body = One click rearranges the editor for the job: Edit, Colour, Audio, VFX, Motion graphics or Production. Alt and 1 to 6 do the same from the keyboard.
tour-ai-title = The AI editor
tour-ai-body = Press ⌘K and say what you want in plain words: cut the pauses, add captions, match the colour. You see every change as it happens. Undo this request, in the panel, takes back what it did; ⌘Z undoes only your own edits.
tour-export-title = Export
tour-export-body = When you are happy, Export makes the finished video for the web, social apps or archive.
tour-help-title = Help is one key away
tour-help-body = Press F1 to search the help. It covers every part of Zornov, and the AI editor can answer questions from it too.

# --- Tips
tip-start-templates = New here? Start from a template below, or open Learn by doing for a guided project.
tip-empty-timeline = Drag media here, or press the plus on a Library item to add it at the playhead.
tip-select-clip = Click a clip to select it. Its settings appear in the Inspector.
tip-split = Press S to split the selected clip at the playhead. Press Delete to remove a piece.
tip-undo = Every change can be undone: ⌘Z undoes, ⇧⌘Z redoes.
tip-ai = Press ⌘K to ask the AI editor: for example, cut the pauses or add captions.
tip-workspaces = Try the workspaces in the top bar, or Alt and 1 to 6, to switch between editing, colour, audio and effects.
tip-keyboard = Everything works from the keyboard. Press F1 and search keyboard for the full list.

# --- Workspaces
workspace-edit-blurb = Cut and arrange: a big timeline with your media beside it.

# --- Help articles
help-start-title = Getting started
help-start-keys = begin first new project welcome tour overview basics
help-start-body = Zornov edits video on a timeline. Make a project from a template, open a sample, or start empty, then bring in video, pictures and sound with Import media in the Library.
    Drag clips onto the timeline or press the plus on a Library item. Press Space to play, S to split, M to add a marker and ⌘Z to undo anything.
    Press ⌘K to ask the AI editor to do a job in plain words. Press F1 whenever you want help.
help-templates-title = Templates and sample projects
help-templates-keys = template youtube short film music video animated story documentary podcast ad canvas aspect ratio sample practice
help-templates-body = On the home screen, Start from a template gives you a project with the right size, frame rate, lanes and markers for a kind of video: YouTube video, short film, music video, animated story, documentary, podcast or ad. Replace the placeholder titles and drop your media into the lanes.
    Learn by doing opens a sample project with steps marked on the timeline. Follow the markers to practise cutting, colour, titles and audio.
help-import-title = Bringing in media
help-import-keys = import media files video photos audio music drag drop folder library download link
help-import-body = Choose File, Import media (⌘I), or drag files into the Library. Zornov keeps your originals where they are and works from them. Formats it cannot play directly are converted for you.
    The Download from a link button fetches media from a page when you have the right to use it. Use Add sample media to try things without your own footage.
help-timeline-title = The timeline
help-timeline-keys = timeline lanes clips playhead zoom snap magnetic markers range select move drag
help-timeline-body = Clips sit on lanes. The Main lane holds the story and closes gaps by itself; other lanes hold titles, overlays and sound wherever you put them. Drag clips to move them, drag an edge to trim.
    Click the ruler to place the playhead. The left and right arrows step a frame, Shift with them steps a second, Home and End go to the ends. N turns snapping on and off. Command with plus and minus zooms, Shift and Z fits the whole edit.
    Press M to add a marker. Press I and O to set the in and out points of a range to loop or export.
help-split-trim-title = Cutting, splitting and trimming
help-split-trim-keys = split cut blade trim slip delete ripple remove two pieces divide shorten
help-split-trim-body = Put the playhead where you want the cut and press S. The selected clip, or every clip under the playhead, is split in two. Press B for the blade tool and click a clip to cut it there. With a trim point set, [ and ] trim the edit back and forward; without one, they select the previous and next clip.
    Drag the edge of a clip to trim it. The Y key switches to slip, which changes which part of the source you see without moving the clip. Select a piece and press Delete to remove it; on the Main lane the gap closes.
help-titles-title = Titles and text
help-titles-keys = title text caption lower third font style size colour outline text style
help-titles-body = Open the Text section of the Library and click a style to add a title at the playhead. Select it and type in the Inspector, Text tab. You can change size, colour, spacing and alignment there.
    Titles are clips on their own lane, so you can move, trim and animate them like any other clip. Turn on Safe areas in the viewer to keep text away from the edges.
help-motion-title = Motion and transitions
help-motion-keys = motion animation entry transition dissolve push dip fade animate move scale rotate
help-motion-body = In the Library, Motions give a clip an entry animation and Cuts add a transition between two clips. Click one to apply it to the selected clip.
    For your own animation use keyframes: the Animation tab of the Inspector has the properties, and the AI editor can animate things when you describe them.
help-effects-title = Effects and looks
help-effects-keys = effects looks blur glow filter adjustment layer stabilize noise reduce apply remove
help-effects-body = Effects change how a clip looks or moves. Click an effect in the Library to add it to the selected clip, or add it as an adjustment clip to affect everything beneath it. The Inspector, Adjust tab lists the effects on a clip with their settings.
    A look is a ready-made colour treatment. Turning an effect off keeps its settings so you can compare.
help-colour-title = Colour and scopes
help-colour-keys = colour color grade grading exposure contrast saturation temperature tint look scopes waveform vectorscope histogram match
help-colour-body = Select a clip and open the Inspector, Adjust tab to change exposure, contrast, saturation, temperature and tint. Looks in the Library apply a whole treatment at once.
    Switch to the Colour workspace for a layout built for grading, with the scopes on. The scopes read the picture you are looking at, so you can judge brightness and colour by numbers as well as by eye. Match colour makes a shot follow a reference shot.
help-audio-title = Audio
help-audio-keys = audio sound volume pan fade music voice mute loudness level mix noise voiceover
help-audio-body = Audio clips sit on audio lanes. Select one and use the Inspector, Audio tab for volume, pan and fades. Mute or lock a whole lane with the buttons at its left.
    The Audio workspace gives you a tall timeline and the sound library. The AI editor can clean up speech, balance music under a voice and add sound effects.
help-keyframes-title = Keyframes
help-keyframes-keys = keyframe animate curve ease graph editor animation property over time
help-keyframes-body = A keyframe records a value at a moment. Two or more make the value change smoothly between them. Click the diamond beside a property in the Inspector to add a key at the playhead.
    Keys show as marks on the clip. Right-click one to choose how it eases into the next. The graph editor in the timeline toolbar shows the same animation as curves.
help-masks-title = Masks and cut-outs
help-masks-keys = mask matte cut out remove background green screen roto shape feather crop
help-masks-body = The Mask section limits an effect or a clip to a shape. A cut-out removes the background from a person or an object you pick. Roto draws a path round an object and follows it through the clip.
    All of these run on your computer. Some need a model downloaded under Settings, Models.
help-tracking-title = Tracking and stabilizing
help-tracking-keys = track follow point stabilize shake camera corner pin surface attach
help-tracking-body = Tracking follows a point or a flat surface through the footage so a title, a mask or a graphic stays attached to it. Stabilizing takes camera shake out of a clip.
    Choose the tracking tool for the selected clip, click a detailed point or drag a box over a flat surface, and let it run. You can correct the track at any frame.
help-speed-title = Speed and slow motion
help-speed-keys = speed slow motion fast reverse ramp frame rate freeze optical flow
help-speed-body = The Inspector, Speed tab changes how fast a clip plays, or plays it backwards. Slowed footage repeats frames; smooth slow motion makes the in-between frames so it stays sharp.
    A freeze frame holds one picture for as long as you need.
help-captions-title = Captions and speech
help-captions-keys = captions subtitles transcribe speech words silence pauses filler text voice
help-captions-body = Auto captions turns speech into editable caption clips. The AI editor can also find pauses and filler words to cut, and can search what was said across your projects.
    Captions are titles, so you can restyle them like any other text.
help-ai-editor-title = The AI editor
help-ai-editor-keys = ai editor assistant claude codex chatgpt command k ask prompt plain words automate
help-ai-editor-body = Press ⌘K, or open the AI section of the Library, and describe what you want: cut the pauses, add captions, make it vertical, match the colour between shots. The AI works with the same tools you have, and every request is one undo step.
    Choose which assistant answers under Settings, AI. Zornov tells you what is sent. If you prefer to approve changes first, turn on Ask first.
help-export-title = Exporting
help-export-keys = export render save video file mp4 format quality resolution social youtube share deliver
help-export-body = Press ⌘E or the Export button. Pick a preset for the web, social apps or archive, check the size and quality, and choose where to save. Exports run in the background and the Jobs button in the top bar shows progress.
    Set in and out points with I and O to export only part of the edit.
help-workspaces-title = Workspaces
help-workspaces-keys = workspace layout edit colour audio vfx motion graphics production panels arrange dock docking drag move tab tabs float reset
help-workspaces-body = A workspace arranges the editor for one kind of work. Edit, Colour, Audio, VFX, Motion graphics and Production are in the top bar and in the Layout menu; Alt with 1 to 6 switches from the keyboard. Drag any panel by its header or tab onto another panel to dock it left, right, above or below it, or into it as a tab; Esc cancels. Right-click a header, or press Shift F10 on a panel reached with F6, for the same moves from a menu. Layout ▸ Panels shows and hides panels, Save layout as keeps yours as a workspace, and Reset layout goes back to Zornov’s own.
    A workspace only sets which panels are open and what the Library and Inspector show. You can still resize panels and change anything afterwards.
help-shortcuts-title = Keyboard shortcuts
help-shortcuts-keys = keyboard shortcuts keys hotkeys commands list customise remap
help-shortcuts-body = Space plays and pauses, J K L play backwards, stop and forwards. S splits, M adds a marker, I and O set range points, A B Y R choose tools, N toggles snapping, F fills the screen. Command with Z, shift Z, D, A and E undo, redo, duplicate, select all and export. [ and ] select the previous and next clip. With a trim point set (press T), they trim back and forward instead.
    Settings, Shortcuts lists every shortcut and lets you change them.
help-keyboard-nav-title = Working with the keyboard and a screen reader
help-keyboard-nav-keys = keyboard screen reader voiceover narrator nvda accessibility navigate blind focus tab landmarks announcements
help-keyboard-nav-body = Zornov works with VoiceOver, Narrator and other screen readers, and everything can be done without a mouse. Tab moves between controls; F6 and Shift F6 jump between the panels on screen.
    On the timeline, ] and [ select the next and previous clip, Up and Down arrows jump to the next and previous edit point, Alt with Up and Down moves to the clip on the lane above or below, and Alt with Left and Right nudges the selected clip by a frame (Shift for a second). Alt and the full stop says where the playhead is.
    On the canvas, the full stop and the comma select the layer below and above at the playhead, Alt and the comma lists the layers, and Command with Alt and the arrow keys moves the selected layer by one percent of the picture (add Shift for five percent). Each step is spoken.
    Changes are spoken as they happen. You can turn spoken updates off in Settings, General, Accessibility.
help-accessibility-title = Accessibility settings
help-accessibility-keys = accessibility high contrast colour blind colour vision large text interface size reduce motion screen reader tips
help-accessibility-body = Settings, General has Interface size (up to 200 percent), High contrast, Colour vision palettes for red-green and blue-yellow colour blindness, Reduce motion and Spoken updates.
    High contrast uses black or white backgrounds with pure text and strong outlines. The colour vision palettes keep clip and status colours apart.
help-language-title = Language
help-language-keys = language translation english hindi spanish french german japanese chinese arabic persian farsi right to left rtl
help-language-body = Zornov is available in English, Hindi, Spanish, French, German, Japanese, Simplified Chinese, Arabic and Persian. Choose one under Settings, General, Language. System default follows your computer.
    Arabic and Persian lay the editor out right to left. The timeline always runs left to right, as time does.
help-saving-title = Saving and projects
help-saving-keys = save open project folder autosave backup recent rename copy file
help-saving-body = A project is a folder. Zornov saves automatically 30 seconds after the last change and keeps 20 backups. Use File, Open to open a project folder, and rename a project by double-clicking its name in the top bar.
    Your media is not copied into the project; keep it where it is.
help-undo-title = Undo and redo
help-undo-keys = undo redo history mistake revert change back
help-undo-body = ⌘Z undoes your last change and ⇧⌘Z redoes it, as many steps as you need. ⌘Z undoes only your own edits: to take back what the AI editor did for a request, press Undo this request in its panel, which undoes the whole request in one step. A toast tells you what was undone.
help-problems-title = When something is slow or does not work
help-problems-keys = slow lag playback dropped frames error problem cannot fails crash proxies cache quality preview
help-problems-body = If playback stutters, lower the preview quality in Settings, Playback, or switch to the simple preview. Long projects benefit from a bigger frame cache.
    If a file will not play, Zornov converts it to a format it can; wait for the job in the top bar to finish. If you hit a crash, Zornov asks before sending a report, and a report is sent only if you choose Send.

